  "commonPitfalls": [
    "Café-au-lait macules in isolation are often misattributed to NF1 without meeting full diagnostic criteria.",
    "Freckling in axillary or inguinal regions may be overlooked, especially in young children.",
    "Lisch nodules require slit-lamp examination and are easily missed on routine ophthalmologic exam.",
    "Cutaneous neurofibromas may not appear until adolescence or adulthood, leading to delayed diagnosis."
  ],
